# A build context is not a private place. Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the
# daemon and cached, so the token must never enter it — even though the final image copies
# only /mp-bot out of the builder and could not leak it anyway. Two independent reasons to
# keep it out, and the weaker one is the one people rely on.
.env

# Nothing the build needs, and the largest thing in the repo.
.git
.gitignore

# Gitignored and unbacked-up. Irrelevant to compiling a binary.
docs/
.claude/

# ⚠️ Test files are deliberately NOT excluded. `go build ./cmd/mp-bot` never compiles a
# _test.go file, so leaving them out could not change the binary — the only effect would be
# to quietly foreclose a `RUN go test ./...` step in the builder stage. This file earns its
# keep on secrets and bulk, not on tidiness.
